---
description: Visual rules for the single demo screen
globs: static/**
alwaysApply: false
---

The screen must read as institutional software, like a terminal view at a bank or a research tool, not a template.

- Use only the CSS variables already in `static/style.css`. One accent colour (`--accent`). Outcome colours only for the outcome label.
- No gradients, glows, emoji, icons-as-decoration, rounded cards with shadows, or hero illustrations.
- Hierarchy through size, weight, and hairline rules (`1px solid var(--rule)`), not boxes.
- Numbers use tabular figures. Show units and sample sizes next to numbers.
- Everything a judge needs must be visible at 1440x900 without scrolling: input, outcome, evidence, the evaluation strip.
- Labels in sentence case. Uppercase only for the small section headings that already use it.
- Loading and error states are one short line of muted text. Never a spinner overlay or a modal.
